      "# Sindh Job Portal 2026: Junior Clerk Vacancies Aur Online Application Ka Tarika",
      "> [!WARNING]\n> **Editorial Hold — Verification Notice:**\n> While the Government of Sindh has established the centralized **Sindh Job Portal (`sjp.gos.pk`)** to streamline provincial hiring, active recruitment schedules for Junior Clerk (BPS-11) positions are announced independently by individual government departments (such as Population Welfare, School Education, Labour, and Law).\n> \n> **Candidates are strongly advised to verify current department-specific advertisements and closing dates on the live portal before paying any testing or application fees.** This guide explains the official application workflow and standard statutory requirements.",
      "## Overview of the Sindh Job Portal (sjp.gos.pk)",
      "The Government of Sindh launched the **Sindh Job Portal** at [sjp.gos.pk](https://sjp.gos.pk/) to unify provincial recruitment across public departments. The platform allows job seekers residing in Sindh to create an official candidate profile, upload their educational credentials, and apply electronically for advertised positions.",
      "## Standard Eligibility Criteria for Junior Clerk (BPS-11)",
      "While specific advertisements govern each hiring cycle, provincial civil service rules for Junior Clerk (BPS-11) in Sindh typically require:\n\n1. **Academic Qualification:**\n   - Higher Secondary School Certificate (Intermediate, 12 years of education) in at least 2nd Division, OR\n   - Bachelor's Degree (Graduation) from an HEC-recognized university (preferred by several departments).\n2. **Computer Proficiency:**\n   - Mandatory minimum 6-month Certificate in **MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint)** from an institute recognized by the **Sindh Board of Technical Education (SBTE)** or Trade Testing Board (TTB).\n3. **Typing Speed:**\n   - Minimum typing speed of **30 words per minute (wpm)** on computer keyboard, tested during post-screening skill assessments.\n4. **Screening Test Qualification:**\n   - For departments utilizing third-party testing services (such as **Sukkur IBA Testing Service - STS**), candidates must meet the minimum passing threshold (typically 40% or 50% in the relevant category).\n5. **Domicile & Age Limit:**\n   - Must hold a valid Domicile and Permanent Resident Certificate (PRC / Form D) of Sindh.\n   - Age limit generally ranges from **18 to 28 years**, with standard upper age relaxation applicable under Sindh Government rules.",
