    "title": "UET Reciprocal Admissions 2026 – 40 Engineering Seats Available",
    "category": "admissions",
    "organization": "University of Engineering and Technology (UET) Lahore",
    "jobType": "Undergraduate Engineering Admissions (Reciprocal Quota Basis)",
    "location": "UET Lahore / Reciprocal Engineering Universities in Sindh, KP, AJK & Balochistan",
    "qualification": "FSc Pre-Engineering / DAE / Equivalent (Min 60% Marks) + UET ECAT 2026",
    "salary": "40 Reserved Undergraduate Engineering Seats (Punjab Domicile Quota)",
    "experience": "Entry Session 2026 Candidates",
    "positions": "40 Engineering Seats",
    "lastDate": "2026-10-09",
    "noDeadline": false,
    "publishDate": "2026-10-05",
    "officialLink": "https://apply.uet.edu.pk/news/83",
    "applyLink": "https://admission.uet.edu.pk/",
    "isVerified": true,
    "featured": true,
    "logoInitial": "UET",
    "featuredImage": "/images/uet-reciprocal-admissions-2026.jpg",
    "imageAlt": "UET Reciprocal Admissions 2026 – 40 Engineering Seats Available — University of Engineering and Technology (UET) Lahore Official Notice CareerDost",
    "excerpt": "UET Lahore invites applications from Punjab domicile holders for 40 reserved undergraduate engineering seats in public universities across Sindh, KP, AJK, and Balochistan on a reciprocal basis for Entry Session 2026. Deadline is 09 October 2026 at 4:00 PM.",
    "content": [
      "### Understanding Reciprocal Engineering Admissions",
      "Under inter-provincial educational exchange treaties, public engineering universities in Pakistan allocate a designated quota of seats for students from other provinces on a mutual **reciprocal basis**. The **University of Engineering and Technology (UET) Lahore** coordinates and administers the selection process for all **Punjab domicile holders** aspiring to secure admission into undergraduate engineering programs in sister universities located in Sindh, Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, Azad Jammu & Kashmir, and Balochistan for **Entry Session 2026**.",
      "According to the official announcement released on the UET Lahore Admissions portal (`apply.uet.edu.pk/news/83`), a total of **40 reserved engineering seats** are available across six prominent engineering institutions.",
      "### Quick Information Summary Table",
      "- **Administering University:** University of Engineering and Technology (UET) Lahore\n- **Intake Category:** Undergraduate Admissions on Reciprocal Basis (Entry Session 2026)\n- **Total Reserved Seats:** 40 Engineering Seats\n- **Eligible Candidates:** Punjab Domicile Holders Only\n- **Mandatory Entrance Exam:** UET Combined Entry Test (ECAT 2026 — March/April or June Session)\n- **Minimum Academic Qualification:** Intermediate Pre-Engineering / DAE with at least 60% Marks\n- **Application Processing Fee:** Rs. 3,000/- per University Preference\n- **Application Form Availability:** Online at [admission.uet.edu.pk](https://admission.uet.edu.pk/)\n- **Submission Mode:** In-Person Submission at Students Section, UET Lahore Main Campus (No Postal / Courier)\n- **Application Deadline:** 09 October 2026 (Friday) at 4:00 PM\n- **Hafiz-e-Quran Test Date:** 15 October 2026 at 10:00 AM\n- **Official Notification Source:** [apply.uet.edu.pk/news/83](https://apply.uet.edu.pk/news/83)",
      "### Complete Breakdown of 40 Reciprocal Engineering Seats",
      "The 40 reciprocal seats are strictly divided among the following six prestigious universities:\n\n1. **NED University of Engineering and Technology, Karachi (04 Seats):**\n   - Electrical Engineering: 02 Seats\n   - Mechanical Engineering: 02 Seats\n\n2. **Mehran University of Engineering and Technology (MUET), Jamshoro (03 Seats):**\n   - Civil Engineering: 01 Seat\n   - Chemical Engineering: 02 Seats\n\n3. **University of Engineering and Technology (UET), Peshawar (10 Seats):**\n   - Civil Engineering: 02 Seats\n   - Electrical Engineering: 02 Seats\n   - Mechanical Engineering: 02 Seats\n   - Mining Engineering: 03 Seats\n   - Agricultural Engineering: 01 Seat\n\n4. **Mirpur University of Engineering & Technology (MUST), Mirpur, AJK (11 Seats):**\n   - Electrical Engineering: 03 Seats\n   - Mechanical Engineering: 02 Seats\n   - Computer System Engineering: 02 Seats\n   - Civil Engineering: 02 Seats\n   - Software Engineering: 02 Seats\n\n5. **Balochistan University of Engineering and Technology (BUET), Khuzdar (09 Seats):**\n   - Civil Engineering: 02 Seats\n   - Electrical Engineering: 03 Seats\n   - Mechanical Engineering: 04 Seats\n\n6. **Dawood University of Engineering & Technology, Karachi (03 Seats):**\n   - Electronics Engineering: 01 Seat\n   - Telecommunication Engineering: 01 Seat\n   - Energy & Environmental Engineering: 01 Seat",
      "### Academic Eligibility & Merit Formula",
      "To qualify for admission consideration against the reciprocal seat quota, candidates must satisfy the following criteria:\n- **Entrance Test Requirement:** Candidates must have appeared in either the First Combined Entry Test 2026 (held from 30 March to 03 April 2026) or the Second ECAT (held from 16 to 21 June 2026) administered by UET Lahore.\n- **Intermediate / DAE Marks:** Minimum **60% aggregate marks** in FSc (Pre-Engineering), relevant Diploma of Associate Engineering (DAE), or equivalent qualification recognized by IBCC.\n- **Official Merit Calculation Weightage:**\n  - **Intermediate / Equivalent Marks:** 70% Weightage\n  - **UET Entry Test (ECAT) Marks:** 30% Weightage\n- **Hafiz-e-Quran Assessment:** Candidates claiming Hafiz-e-Quran additional marks who did not appear in the test on 17 or 18 July 2026 must appear for the test on **15 October 2026 at 10:00 AM**.",
      "### Step-by-Step Application Procedure",
      "> [!WARNING]\n> **In-Person Submission Only:** UET Lahore explicitly mandates that application forms must be submitted by hand at the UET Lahore Administration Block. Submissions sent via Pakistan Post, courier, or delivery services **will NOT be entertained**.\n\n1. **Online Form Generation:** Visit `https://admission.uet.edu.pk/` and fill out the reciprocal admission application form.\n2. **Generate Bank Challan:** Print the computerized bank challan for the preference fee of **Rs. 3,000/- per university** and deposit the amount at designated bank branches.\n3. **Print Completed Form:** Print a physical copy of the filled application form and sign the declarations.\n4. **Attach Required Documents:** Attach certified copies of Punjab Domicile, Matric certificate, Intermediate DMC / DAE transcript, ECAT result card, and original bank payment slip.\n5. **Submit at UET Lahore:** Visit the **Students Section (Administration Block), UET Lahore**, on any working day between **9:00 AM and 3:30 PM**.\n6. **Submission Deadline:** Ensure your application is deposited before **09 October 2026 (Friday) at 4:00 PM**.",
      "### Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)",
      "**Q1: What is the deadline to submit the UET Reciprocal Admission form?**\nThe final closing date and time for receipt of applications at UET Lahore is **09 October 2026 (Friday) at 4:00 PM**.\n\n**Q2: Can applicants from other provinces apply through this quota?**\nNo. This reciprocal quota is exclusively reserved for candidates holding a valid **Punjab domicile**.\n\n**Q3: Can I send my application by courier or post?**\nNo. UET Lahore strictly requires physical in-person submission at the Students Section, Administration Block, UET Lahore.\n\n**Q4: How many reciprocal engineering seats are available in total?**\nExactly **40 seats** are available across six universities (NED, MUET, UET Peshawar, MUST, BUET Khuzdar, and Dawood UET).\n\n**Q5: What is the processing fee per university preference?**\nThe application fee is **Rs. 3,000/- per university** applied for.\n\n**Q6: What is the aggregate merit formula for reciprocal seats?**\nMerit is calculated based on **70% Intermediate marks** and **30% UET Entry Test (ECAT) score**."
    ],
